    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0443" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1448.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 25th of May, (No.
                    967,) which is accompanied by a copy of a note of the 19th ultimo, addressed to
                    you by Earl Russell, relative to demands made by the United States on the
                    governor of the Bahamas for the extradition of Vernon Locke, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM HUNTER. <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
